        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(sessions): bound trajectory snapshot and pointer reads",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`readTrajectorySnapshot` in `src/commands/sessions-tail.ts` loaded the entire trajectory JSONL file with `fs.readFileSync(filePath, \"utf8\")` and no size cap. `openclaw sessions tail` on a rotated or runaway trajectory file could OOM before rendering any events. The trajectory pointer reader also used an unbounded `fs.readFileSync` for a small JSON file.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Trajectory snapshots are rendered into recent events; 16 MiB is generous headroom for busy sessions while bounding memory.\n- Trajectory pointer files are tiny JSON envelopes, so a 64 KiB cap is ample.\n- Both reads now use the shared `readRegularFileSync` helper, which verifies the path is a regular file and cancels on overflow.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- `openclaw sessions tail` no longer buffers arbitrarily large trajectory files.\n- Oversized trajectory snapshots fail with a clear size-limit error instead of crashing.\n- Normal tail usage is unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Replaced unbounded `fs.readFileSync` calls with `readRegularFileSync` capped reads in `src/commands/sessions-tail.ts`.\n- Added a regression test in `src/commands/sessions-tail.test.ts` asserting that a snapshot exceeding 16 MiB is rejected.\n- Lint and core typecheck pass locally. Full test suite will run on the PR CI.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nI created a temporary session store with one running session and exercised `openclaw sessions tail` against a normal trajectory snapshot and an oversized snapshot (50 MiB + 1 byte, i.e. `TRAJECTORY_RUNTIME_FILE_MAX_BYTES + 1`).\n\nNormal snapshot renders the event and exits cleanly:\n\n```text\n$ OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR=/tmp/proof-101450/state \\\n  node scripts/run-node.mjs sessions tail \\\n  --store /tmp/proof-101450/sessions.json \\\n  --session-key agent:main:telegram:direct:owner \\\n  --tail 5\n12:04:17 session.started  agent:main:telegram:direct:ow… session started\n# exit code: 0\n```\n\nOversized snapshot is rejected before any parsing or rendering, and the command exits non-zero:\n\n```text\n$ OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR=/tmp/proof-101450/state \\\n  node scripts/run-node.mjs sessions tail \\\n  --store /tmp/proof-101450/sessions.json \\\n  --session-key agent:main:telegram:direct:owner \\\n  --tail 5\nError: File exceeds 52428800 bytes: /tmp/proof-101450/session-one.trajectory.jsonl\n# exit code: 1\n```\n\nThe bounded read (`readRegularFileSync` with `maxBytes: TRAJECTORY_RUNTIME_FILE_MAX_BYTES`) stops the tail command from buffering the oversized trajectory file; no trajectory events are parsed or printed, and no downstream network calls occur.\n",
        "branch": "fix/bound-sessions-tail-snapshot-reads",
